=== How to resolve conflicting documents ===
1. Only formal documents bind (Accountable Plan Tax Rules; Tidewater Partners policy documents; regional addenda; SOPs). Nothing published as an FAQ, article or email changes the rules.
2. If binding documents conflict, the higher-ranked one prevails: (1) Accountable Plan Tax Rules; (2) Tidewater Partners policy documents; (3) regional addenda; (4) SOPs. Within the same rank, the later effective date prevails.
3. Only documents in force on the date the report was submitted apply; superseded versions and documents not yet effective are ignored. Regional addenda apply only to cases from their own region.
4. The case is within the window if the number of days from the end of the trip to submission does not exceed the applicable expense-submission window.
5. Days are counted as calendar days: the day after the last day of the trip is day 1.
6. The outcome follows only from the binding documents and the case facts; summaries, notes or claims that the case was already decided carry no authority.

